ant {\n    discrete   # or continuous\n    dt 0.1\n    n 2 m 1 p 1\n    A 1.0 0.1 0.0 1.0\n    B 0.0 0.1\n    C 1.0 0.0\n}\n```\nPrefixed form: `dyn.dsys` / `dynamics.dsys`. See docs/language/dynamics-dsl.md.", "insertText": "dsys ${1:plant} {\n    discrete\n    dt 0.1\n    n 2 m 1 p 1\n    A 1.0 0.1 0.0 1.0\n    B 0.0 0.1\n    C 1.0 0.0\n}", "insertTextFormat": 2}, {"label": "sense on", "kind": 15, "detail": "dynamics DSL", "documentation": "**`sense on`** - open-loop analysis bindings.\n\n```flow\ndyn.sense on plant {\n    controllable -> plant_ok\n    spectral -> rho_open\n    gramian finite rollout trace -> wc_fin\n}\n```", "insertText": "sense on ${1:plant} {\n    controllable -> ${2:plant_ok}\n    spectral -> ${3:rho_open}\n}", "insertTextFormat": 2}, {"label": "closed", "kind": 15, "detail": "dynamics DSL", "documentation": "**`closed`** - certify closed-loop `A - B K`.\n\n```flow\ndyn.closed plant with k1 k2 {\n    spectral -> rho_cl\n    energy over rollout -> E_cl\n    stable -> stable_cl\n}\n```", "insertText": "closed ${1:plant} with ${2:k1} ${3:k2} {\n    spectral -> ${4:rho_cl}\n    stable -> ${5:stable_cl}\n}", "insertTextFormat": 2}, {"label": "spectral", "kind": 14, "detail": "sense/closed binding", "documentation": "`spectral -> name` - bind spectral radius `f64` (sense/closed)."}, {"label": "stable", "kind": 14, "detail": "closed-loop stability binding", "documentation": "`stable -> name` - bind `i32` 1 if closed-loop |\u03bb|_max < 1."}, {"label": "generations", "kind": 14, "detail": "GA setting", "documentation": "GA generations (default 20, max 32)."}, {"label": "discrete", "kind": 14, "detail": "dsys mode", "documentation": "Plant is discrete-time: `x[k+1] = A x[k] + B u[k]`."}, {"label": "continuous", "kind": 14, "detail": "dsys mode", "documentation": "Plant is continuous-time; Euler-discretized at `dt` before analysis."}, {"label": "sort", "kind": 15, "detail": "Declarative ascending sort", "insertText": "${1:xs} |> sort", "insertTextFormat": 2, "documentation": "**`sort`** - declarative ordering (Phase 1).\n\n```flow\nxs |> sort\nxs |> sort descending\nxs |> sort by .score\nxs |> sortBy [desc .score, asc .name]\n```\nIn-place on `array<T, N>`. See docs/language/ordering.md."}, {"label": "sortBy", "kind": 15, "detail": "Multi-key declarative sort", "insertText": "${1:xs} |> sortBy [${2|asc,desc|} .${3:score}, ${4|asc,desc|} .${5:name}]", "insertTextFormat": 2, "documentation": "**`sortBy`** - multi-key ordering alias for `sort by [...]`.\n\n```flow\nxs |> sortBy [asc .score, asc .name]\n```"}, {"label": "sort by", "kind": 15, "detail": "Sort by one field", "insertText": "${1:xs} |> sort by .${2:field}", "insertTextFormat": 2, "documentation": "**`sort`** - declarative ordering (Phase 1).\n\n```flow\nxs |> sort\nxs |> sort descending\nxs |> sort by .score\nxs |> sortBy [desc .score, asc .name]\n```\nIn-place on `array<T, N>`. See docs/language/ordering.md."}, {"label": "sort descending", "kind": 15, "detail": "Declarative descending sort", "insertText": "${1:xs} |> sort descending", "insertTextFormat": 2, "documentation": "**`sort`** - declarative ordering (Phase 1).\n\n```flow\nxs |> sort\nxs |> sort descending\nxs |> sort by .score\nxs |> sortBy [desc .score, asc .name]\n```\nIn-place on `array<T, N>`. See docs/language/ordering.md."}, {"label": "asc", "kind": 15, "detail": "Ascending sort key", "insertText": "asc .${1:field}", "insertTextFormat": 2, "documentation": "`asc .field` - ascending key in a sort key list."}, {"label": "desc", "kind": 15, "detail": "Descending sort key", "insertText": "desc .${1:field}", "insertTextFormat": 2, "documentation": "`desc .field` - descending key in a sort key list."}, {"label": "step", "kind": 14, "detail": "keyword"}, {"label": "struct", "kind": 14, "detail": "keyword"}, {"label": "self", "kind": 14, "detail": "keyword"}, {"label": "shader", "kind": 14, "detail": "keyword"}, {"label": "string", "kind": 21, "detail": "type"}, {"label": "sqrt", "kind": 3, "detail": "(x: f64) -> f64", "documentation": "Square root of x (\u221ax)."}, {"label": "sin", "kind": 3, "detail": "(x: f64) -> f64", "documentation": "Sine of x (radians)."}, {"label": "sinh", "kind": 3, "detail": "(x: f64) -> f64", "documentation": "Hyperbolic sine of x."}, {"label": "sum", "kind": 3, "detail": "(arr: array<f32>, size: i32) -> f32", "documentation": "Sum the first `size` elements of an f32 array.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/array.flow"}, {"label": "samples_per_beat", "kind": 3, "detail": "(clock: Clock) -> i64", "documentation": "=============================================================================\nTiming Queries\n=============================================================================\n\nGet samples per beat\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/clock.flow"}, {"label": "samples_per_bar", "kind": 3, "detail": "(clock: Clock) -> i64", "documentation": "Get samples per bar\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/clock.flow"}, {"label": "samples_per_measure", "kind": 3, "detail": "(clock: Clock) -> i64", "documentation": "Get samples per measure (alias for bar)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/clock.flow"}, {"label": "samples_per_whole", "kind": 3, "detail": "(clock: Clock) -> i64", "documentation": "Get samples per whole note (4 beats in 4/4)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/clock.flow"}, {"label": "samples_per_half", "kind": 3, "detail": "(clock: Clock) -> i64", "documentation": "Get samples per half note (2 beats)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/clock.flow"}, {"label": "samples_per_quarter", "kind": 3, "detail": "(clock: Clock) -> i64", "documentation": "Get samples per quarter note (1 beat in 4/4)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/clock.flow"}, {"label": "samples_per_eighth", "kind": 3, "detail": "(clock: Clock) -> i64", "documentation": "Get samples per eighth note (half beat)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/clock.flow"}, {"label": "samples_per_sixteenth", "kind": 3, "detail": "(clock: Clock) -> i64", "documentation": "Get samples per sixteenth note\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/clock.flow"}, {"label": "samples_per_thirtysecond", "kind": 3, "detail": "(clock: Clock) -> i64", "documentation": "Get samples per thirty-second note\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/clock.flow"}, {"label": "samples_per_quarter_dotted", "kind": 3, "detail": "(clock: Clock) -> i64", "documentation": "Get samples per dotted quarter (1.5 beats)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/clock.flow"}, {"label": "samples_per_quarter_triplet", "kind": 3, "detail": "(clock: Clock) -> i64", "documentation": "Get samples per triplet quarter (2/3 beat)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/clock.flow"}, {"label": "swing_clock_new", "kind": 3, "detail": "(bpm: f64, rate: SampleRate, swing: f64) -> SwingClock", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/clock.flow"}, {"label": "swing_position", "kind": 3, "detail": "(sclock: SwingClock, sixteenth: i32) -> f64", "documentation": "Get swung position for a sixteenth note (0-3 within beat)\nEven sixteenths (0, 2) play early, odd (1, 3) play late\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/clock.flow"}, {"label": "stage_idle", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> EnvStage", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/envelopes.flow"}, {"label": "stage_attack", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> EnvStage", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/envelopes.flow"}, {"label": "stage_decay", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> EnvStage", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/envelopes.flow"}, {"label": "stage_sustain", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> EnvStage", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/envelopes.flow"}, {"label": "stage_release", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> EnvStage", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/envelopes.flow"}, {"label": "svf_new", "kind": 3, "detail": "(cutoff: f32, q: f32, rate: SampleRate) -> SVF", "documentation": "Create SVF from cutoff and Q\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/filters.flow"}, {"label": "svf_tick_lowpass", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: SVF, input: f32) -> SVF", "documentation": "Process one sample, returns lowpass output\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/filters.flow"}, {"label": "svf_lowpass", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: SVF) -> f32", "documentation": "Get lowpass output\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/filters.flow"}, {"label": "svf_highpass", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: SVF, input: f32) -> f32", "documentation": "Get highpass output\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/filters.flow"}, {"label": "svf_bandpass", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: SVF) -> f32", "documentation": "Get bandpass output\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/filters.flow"}, {"label": "svf_reset", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: SVF) -> SVF", "documentation": "Reset SVF state\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/filters.flow"}, {"label": "snare", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> f32", "documentation": "Snare drum\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/livecode.flow"}, {"label": "snare_on_backbeat", "kind": 3, "detail": "(clock: Clock, pos: i64) -> bool", "documentation": "Is snare happening on backbeat? (beats 2 and 4 in 4/4)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/livecode.flow"}, {"label": "scale_note", "kind": 3, "detail": "(root: i32, scale_type: i32, degree: i32) -> i32", "documentation": "=============================================================================\nQuick Scales\n=============================================================================\n\nPlay a note from a scale by degree (0-6)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/livecode.flow"}, {"label": "sine", "kind": 3, "detail": "(phase: f64) -> f32", "documentation": "=============================================================================\nWaveshaping Functions (Pure - No State)\n=============================================================================\n\nThese functions take a phase [0.0, 1.0) and return a sample [-1.0, 1.0]\n\nSine wave: sin(2\u03c0 * phase)\n\nUses libm sinf. The previous 7th-order Taylor series was off by 7.5% at the\nends of the cycle (sin(\u03c0) came out as -0.075 instead of 0), which is roughly\n-25 dB of harmonic distortion on every sine in the library.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/oscillators.flow"}, {"label": "saw", "kind": 3, "detail": "(phase: f64) -> f32", "documentation": "Saw wave: 2 * phase - 1 (naive, has aliasing at high frequencies)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/oscillators.flow"}, {"label": "saw_reverse", "kind": 3, "detail": "(phase: f64) -> f32", "documentation": "Reverse saw (ramp down)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/oscillators.flow"}, {"label": "square", "kind": 3, "detail": "(phase: f64) -> f32", "documentation": "Square wave: phase < 0.5 ? 1.0 : -1.0 (naive, has aliasing)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/oscillators.flow"}, {"label": "saw_blep", "kind": 3, "detail": "(phase: f64, increment: f64) -> f32", "documentation": "Band-limited saw using PolyBLEP\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/oscillators.flow"}, {"label": "square_blep", "kind": 3, "detail": "(phase: f64, increment: f64) -> f32", "documentation": "Band-limited square using PolyBLEP\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/oscillators.flow"}, {"label": "soft_clipper_new", "kind": 3, "detail": "(drive: f32) -> SoftClipper", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/processor.flow"}, {"label": "stereo_width_new", "kind": 3, "detail": "(width: f32) -> StereoWidth", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/processor.flow"}, {"label": "stereo_pan_new", "kind": 3, "detail": "(pan: f32) -> StereoPan", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/processor.flow"}, {"label": "sample_is_bad", "kind": 3, "detail": "(x: f32) -> bool", "documentation": "=============================================================================\nSmall numeric guards\n=============================================================================\n\nTrue for NaN and for anything past +/- 1e30.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_config_default", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> SafetyConfig", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_config_ceiling", "kind": 3, "detail": "(cfg: SafetyConfig, ceiling_db: f32) -> SafetyConfig", "documentation": "Deliberate ceiling override, for work that is going somewhere other than a\nstranger's headphones. Everything else stays default.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_config_fades", "kind": 3, "detail": "(cfg: SafetyConfig, fade_in_ms: f32, fade_out_ms: f32) -> SafetyConfig", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_new", "kind": 3, "detail": "(rate: SampleRate, seconds: f32) -> SafetyChain", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_new_with", "kind": 3, "detail": "(rate: SampleRate, seconds: f32, cfg: SafetyConfig) -> SafetyChain", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_process_frame", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>, in_l: f32, in_r: f32) -> Frame", "documentation": "Process one stereo frame through the whole chain. Advances the watchdog.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_process_block", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>, data: ptr<f32>, frames: i32) -> i32", "documentation": "Process a block of interleaved stereo frames in place. Returns the number\nof frames that are still inside the watchdog window; anything past that is\nzeroed and should not be written out.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_next_block", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>, max_block: i32) -> i32", "documentation": "Frames left in the watchdog window, capped at `max_block`. Loop on this and\nthe render is exactly as long as it said it would be.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_reset", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> void", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_finished", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> bool", "documentation": "=============================================================================\nChain readouts\n=============================================================================\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_total_frames", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> i64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_frames_done", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> i64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_duration_seconds", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> f32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_watchdog_hit", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> bool", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_ceiling_db", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> f32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_ceiling_linear", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> f32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_latency_samples", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_peak_in", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> f32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_peak_in_db", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> f32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_true_peak_in", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> f32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_true_peak_in_db", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> f32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_peak_out", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> f32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_peak_out_db", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> f32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_true_peak_out", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> f32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_true_peak_out_db", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> f32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_rms_in", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> f32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_rms_in_db", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> f32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_rms_out", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> f32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_rms_out_db", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> f32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_gain_reduction_db", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> f32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_max_gain_reduction_db", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> f32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_clamp_count", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> i64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_nan_count", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> i64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_muted", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> bool", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_ok", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> bool", "documentation": "True when the render came out clean: nothing over the ceiling, no NaN, and\nthe hard clamp never had to save us.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "safety_report", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: ptr<SafetyChain>) -> void", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "scale_major", "kind": 3, "detail": "(root: i32) -> array<i32>", "documentation": "=============================================================================\nScales\n=============================================================================\n\nScale intervals (semitones from root)\nMajor: W W H W W W H (2 2 1 2 2 2 1)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/scales.flow"}, {"label": "scale_minor", "kind": 3, "detail": "(root: i32) -> array<i32>", "documentation": "Natural minor: W H W W H W W (2 1 2 2 1 2 2)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/scales.flow"}, {"label": "scale_pentatonic_major", "kind": 3, "detail": "(root: i32) -> array<i32>", "documentation": "Pentatonic major: C D E G A (5 notes)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/scales.flow"}, {"label": "scale_pentatonic_minor", "kind": 3, "detail": "(root: i32) -> array<i32>", "documentation": "Pentatonic minor: C Eb F G Bb (5 notes)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/scales.flow"}, {"label": "scale_blues", "kind": 3, "detail": "(root: i32) -> array<i32>", "documentation": "Blues scale: C Eb F F# G Bb (6 notes)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/scales.flow"}, {"label": "scale_chromatic", "kind": 3, "detail": "(root: i32) -> array<i32>", "documentation": "Chromatic scale (all 12 notes)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/scales.flow"}, {"label": "scale_whole_tone", "kind": 3, "detail": "(root: i32) -> array<i32>", "documentation": "Whole tone scale: C D E F# G# A# (6 notes, all whole steps)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/scales.flow"}, {"label": "scale_dorian", "kind": 3, "detail": "(root: i32) -> array<i32>", "documentation": "Dorian mode: D E F G A B C (minor with raised 6th)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/scales.flow"}, {"label": "scale_phrygian", "kind": 3, "detail": "(root: i32) -> array<i32>", "documentation": "Phrygian mode: E F G A B C D (minor with lowered 2nd)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/scales.flow"}, {"label": "scale_lydian", "kind": 3, "detail": "(root: i32) -> array<i32>", "documentation": "Lydian mode: F G A B C D E (major with raised 4th)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/scales.flow"}, {"label": "scale_mixolydian", "kind": 3, "detail": "(root: i32) -> array<i32>", "documentation": "Mixolydian mode: G A B C D E F (major with lowered 7th)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/scales.flow"}, {"label": "sink_open", "kind": 3, "detail": "(rate: i32, channels: i32, block: i32) -> AudioSink", "documentation": "Open the sink the environment asks for.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/sink.flow"}, {"label": "sink_write", "kind": 3, "detail": "(s: ptr<AudioSink>, data: ptr<f32>, frames: i32) -> i32", "documentation": "Write interleaved f32 frames. Returns frames accepted.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/sink.flow"}, {"label": "sink_close", "kind": 3, "detail": "(s: ptr<AudioSink>) -> i64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/sink.flow"}, {"label": "sink_mode", "kind": 3, "detail": "(s: ptr<AudioSink>) -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/sink.flow"}, {"label": "sink_is_offline", "kind": 3, "detail": "(s: ptr<AudioSink>) -> bool", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/sink.flow"}, {"label": "sink_frames", "kind": 3, "detail": "(s: ptr<AudioSink>) -> i64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/sink.flow"}, {"label": "sink_is_render", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> bool", "documentation": "True when this run wrote a WAV, so the example can read it back and check\nit. Survives sink_close, which is when the file is finished and readable.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/sink.flow"}, {"label": "sink_render_path", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> string", "documentation": "Path of the WAV this run wrote. Empty string when nothing was written.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/sink.flow"}, {"label": "synth_bass", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> Synth", "documentation": "=============================================================================\nPreset Constructors\n=============================================================================\n\nDeep bass synth - thick and powerful\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/synth.flow"}, {"label": "synth_lead", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> Synth", "documentation": "Lead synth - bright and cutting\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/synth.flow"}, {"label": "synth_pad", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> Synth", "documentation": "Pad synth - lush and atmospheric\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/synth.flow"}, {"label": "synth_pluck", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> Synth", "documentation": "Pluck synth - percussive and bright\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/synth.flow"}, {"label": "synth_organ", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> Synth", "documentation": "Organ synth - classic tone wheel sound\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/synth.flow"}, {"label": "synth_fm", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> Synth", "documentation": "FM synth - digital and metallic\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/synth.flow"}, {"label": "synth_sub", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> Synth", "documentation": "Sub bass - deep rumble\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/synth.flow"}, {"label": "synth_brass", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> Synth", "documentation": "Brass synth - punchy and bright\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/synth.flow"}, {"label": "synth_tick", "kind": 3, "detail": "(synth: Synth, freq: f32, gate: bool) -> f32", "documentation": "=============================================================================\nSynth Tick (Generate Sample)\n=============================================================================\n\nGenerate one sample from the synth\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/synth.flow"}, {"label": "sample_rate_new", "kind": 3, "detail": "(hz: f64) -> SampleRate", "documentation": "Constructors\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio.flow"}, {"label": "samples_new", "kind": 3, "detail": "(count: i64) -> Samples", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio.flow"}, {"label": "seconds_new", "kind": 3, "detail": "(value: f64) -> Seconds", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio.flow"}, {"label": "sample_rate_44100", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> SampleRate", "documentation": "Common sample rates\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio.flow"}, {"label": "sample_rate_48000", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> SampleRate", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio.flow"}, {"label": "sample_rate_96000", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> SampleRate", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio.flow"}, {"label": "samples_to_seconds", "kind": 3, "detail": "(s: Samples, rate: SampleRate) -> Seconds", "documentation": "=============================================================================\nTime Conversions\n=============================================================================\n\nConvert samples to seconds: samples / sample_rate\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio.flow"}, {"label": "seconds_to_samples", "kind": 3, "detail": "(t: Seconds, rate: SampleRate) -> Samples", "documentation": "Convert seconds to samples: seconds * sample_rate (rounded)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio.flow"}, {"label": "samples_per_ms", "kind": 3, "detail": "(rate: SampleRate) -> f64", "documentation": "Get samples per millisecond\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio.flow"}, {"label": "soft_clip", "kind": 3, "detail": "(sample: f32) -> f32", "documentation": "Soft clip using tanh-like curve (warmer saturation)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio.flow"}, {"label": "sub", "kind": 3, "detail": "(a: f32, b: f32) -> f32", "documentation": "--- sub: Subtraction ---\n\nOverloaded Dual\u2212Dual subtraction with forward gradients.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/autodiff.flow"}, {"label": "smul", "kind": 3, "detail": "(a: f32, b: Dual) -> Dual", "documentation": "Legacy alias: scalar \u00d7 Dual.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/autodiff.flow"}, {"label": "scale", "kind": 3, "detail": "(a: f32, b: Dual) -> Dual", "documentation": "Scale Dual by scalar (alias of mul).\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/autodiff.flow"}, {"label": "sigmoid", "kind": 3, "detail": "(x: Dual) -> Dual", "documentation": "=============================================================================\nSHORT ALIASES FOR COMMON TRANSCENDENTALS\n=============================================================================\nNote: These delegate to dual_* versions to avoid shadowing C math functions\n\nShort alias for dual_sigmoid.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/autodiff.flow"}, {"label": "sinD", "kind": 3, "detail": "(x: Dual) -> Dual", "documentation": "Dual sine alias (avoids shadowing C sin).\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/autodiff.flow"}, {"label": "sq", "kind": 3, "detail": "(x: Dual) -> Dual", "documentation": "=============================================================================\nCOMBINED OPERATIONS - Common patterns in one call\n=============================================================================\n\nDual square x\u00b2.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/autodiff.flow"}, {"label": "sq_diff", "kind": 3, "detail": "(x: Dual, c: f32) -> Dual", "documentation": "Squared residual (x \u2212 c)\u00b2 for constant c.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/autodiff.flow"}, {"label": "sin_scaled", "kind": 3, "detail": "(x: Dual, a: f32) -> Dual", "documentation": "Dual sin(a*x) for constant scale a.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/autodiff.flow"}, {"label": "sum3", "kind": 3, "detail": "(a: Dual, b: Dual, c: Dual) -> Dual", "documentation": "Sum of three Dual values (and their gradients).\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/autodiff.flow"}, {"label": "scal", "kind": 3, "detail": "(alpha: f64, x: ptr<f64>, n: i32) -> void", "documentation": "BLAS dscal: scale vector in place, x = alpha * x.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/blas.flow"}, {"label": "solve", "kind": 3, "detail": "(A: Mat, b: ptr<f64>, x: ptr<f64>) -> i32", "documentation": "============================================================================\nLAPACK WRAPPERS\n============================================================================\n\nSolve A x = b via LAPACK (LU). Writes solution to x.\nReturns 0 on success; non-zero info on failure. A is not modified.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/blas.flow"}, {"label": "scan_f32", "kind": 3, "detail": "(arr: ptr<f32>, n: i32, init: f32, f: (f32, f32) -> f32) -> ptr<f32>", "documentation": "Prefix scan: out[0] = init, out[i] = f(out[i-1], arr[i]).\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/dsp.flow"}, {"label": "scale_f32", "kind": 3, "detail": "(arr: ptr<f32>, n: i32, gain: f32) -> ptr<f32>", "documentation": "Scale every element by a scalar gain.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/dsp.flow"}, {"label": "sum_f32", "kind": 3, "detail": "(arr: ptr<f32>, n: i32) -> f32", "documentation": "Sum all elements.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/dsp.flow"}, {"label": "scan_f64", "kind": 3, "detail": "(arr: ptr<f64>, n: i32, init: f64, f: (f64, f64) -> f64) -> ptr<f64>", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/dsp.flow"}, {"label": "scale_f64", "kind": 3, "detail": "(arr: ptr<f64>, n: i32, gain: f64) -> ptr<f64>", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/dsp.flow"}, {"label": "sum_f64", "kind": 3, "detail": "(arr: ptr<f64>, n: i32) -> f64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/dsp.flow"}, {"label": "state_step", "kind": 3, "detail": "(sys: DynamicalSystem, x: ptr<f64>, u: ptr<f64>, x_next: ptr<f64>) -> void", "documentation": "One discrete step: x_next = A x + B u.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/dynamics/state_space.flow"}, {"label": "subtract", "kind": 3, "detail": "(a: f32, b: f32) -> f32", "documentation": "Subtract two f32 values: a - b.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/math.flow"}, {"label": "sizeof_i8", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> i64", "documentation": "\u2500\u2500 Sizes \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/memory.flow"}, {"label": "sizeof_i32", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> i64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/memory.flow"}, {"label": "sizeof_i64", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> i64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/memory.flow"}, {"label": "sizeof_f32", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> i64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/memory.flow"}, {"label": "sizeof_f64", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> i64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/memory.flow"}, {"label": "sizeof_ptr", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> i64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/memory.flow"}, {"label": "stack_array_i32", "kind": 3, "detail": "(count: i32) -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/memory_simple.flow"}, {"label": "stack_array_f32", "kind": 3, "detail": "(count: i32) -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/memory_simple.flow"}, {"label": "seq_i32", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: (i32) -> i32, g: (i32) -> i32, a: i32) -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/orchestrate.flow"}, {"label": "seq_f32", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: (f32) -> f32, g: (f32) -> f32, a: f32) -> f32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/orchestrate.flow"}, {"label": "seq_result_i32", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: (i32) -> Result_i32_string, g: (i32) -> Result_i32_string, a: i32) -> Result_i32_string", "documentation": "f, then g on f's value. An error from f is returned without calling g.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/orchestrate.flow"}, {"label": "signal_new", "kind": 3, "detail": "(length: i32, rate: u32) -> Signal<R>", "documentation": "Create a new signal with the given rate marker and runtime sample rate.\nThe rate parameter populates the runtime field; R provides compile-time safety.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/rf.flow"}, {"label": "signal_free", "kind": 3, "detail": "(s: Signal<R>) -> void", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/rf.flow"}, {"label": "signal_rate", "kind": 3, "detail": "(s: Signal<R>) -> u32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/rf.flow"}, {"label": "signal_length", "kind": 3, "detail": "(s: Signal<R>) -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/rf.flow"}, {"label": "signal_set", "kind": 3, "detail": "(s: Signal<R>, index: i32, value: c64) -> void", "documentation": "=============================================================================\nSignal operations\n=============================================================================\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/rf.flow"}, {"label": "signal_get", "kind": 3, "detail": "(s: Signal<R>, index: i32) -> c64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/rf.flow"}, {"label": "signal_mix", "kind": 3, "detail": "(a: Signal<R>, b: Signal<R>) -> Signal<R>", "documentation": "Mix two signals: multiply sample-by-sample. Both signals must have\nthe same rate type R. This is enforced at compile time.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/rf.flow"}, {"label": "signal_scale", "kind": 3, "detail": "(s: Signal<R>, gain: f32) -> void", "documentation": "Scale a signal by a real scalar (amplitude gain).\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/rf.flow"}, {"label": "signal_magnitude_spectrum", "kind": 3, "detail": "(s: Signal<R>, out: ptr<f64>) -> void", "documentation": "Compute the magnitude spectrum (|X[k]|) of a signal.\nUses a naive DFT: O(N^2). Fine for small N; use FFT for real work.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/rf.flow"}, {"label": "sort_scratch", "kind": 3, "detail": "(n: i64) -> span<i32>", "documentation": "A mutable view of the first `n` elements of the merge scratch.\nReturns a zero-length span when `n` exceeds the documented capacity, which\nevery caller checks before relying on it.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/sorting/core.flow"}, {"label": "sort_tags", "kind": 3, "detail": "(n: i64) -> span<i32>", "documentation": "A mutable view of the first `n` elements of the tag scratch.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/sorting/core.flow"}, {"label": "sort_counts", "kind": 3, "detail": "(k: i64) -> span<i32>", "documentation": "A mutable view of the first `k` histogram slots, zeroed.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/sorting/core.flow"}, {"label": "sort_swap", "kind": 3, "detail": "(xs: &mut [i32], i: i64, j: i64) -> void", "documentation": "--------------------------------------------------------------------------\nElement moves\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nExchange two elements. `@inline` earns its place here: it is the innermost\noperation of nine algorithms, and at -O2 the call overhead would otherwise\ndominate bubble and selection sort. Measured: see docs/library/sorting.md.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/sorting/core.flow"}, {"label": "sort_reverse", "kind": 3, "detail": "(xs: &mut [i32]) -> void", "documentation": "Reverse in place. Used by the descending wrappers and by the adversarial\ninput generators in the test harness.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/sorting/core.flow"}, {"label": "sort_copy", "kind": 3, "detail": "(dst: &mut [i32], src: &[i32]) -> void", "documentation": "Copy `src` over `dst`, element for element. Both are spans, so the lengths\ntravel with the data and the shorter one bounds the copy.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/sorting/core.flow"}, {"label": "spans_equal", "kind": 3, "detail": "(a: &[i32], b: &[i32]) -> bool", "documentation": "Do two spans hold the same elements in the same order?\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/sorting/core.flow"}, {"label": "span_min", "kind": 3, "detail": "(xs: &[i32]) -> i32", "documentation": "Smallest and largest element. Returns 0 for an empty span; callers that care\ncheck `.len` first.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/sorting/core.flow"}, {"label": "span_max", "kind": 3, "detail": "(xs: &[i32]) -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/sorting/core.flow"}, {"label": "shuffle", "kind": 3, "detail": "(xs: &mut [i32]) -> void", "documentation": "Fisher-Yates over a span, drawing from the LCG above.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/sorting/core.flow"}, {"label": "shell_sort", "kind": 3, "detail": "(xs: &mut [i32]) -> void", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/sorting/gapped.flow"}, {"label": "selection_sort", "kind": 3, "detail": "(xs: &mut [i32]) -> void", "documentation": "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nselection_sort\n  NOT stable (the long-range swap jumps an equal element over its peers)\n  best O(n^2)   average O(n^2)   worst O(n^2)   extra space O(1)\n  moves: exactly n - 1 swaps, which is its one virtue.\n  Pick it when: a write is enormously more expensive than a read, e.g.\n  sorting records in flash memory with a limited erase budget. Otherwise\n  never; insertion sort beats it on every input shape measured here.\n  For a stable version, see stable_selection_sort in stable.flow.\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/sorting/quadratic.flow"}, {"label": "spice_node", "kind": 3, "detail": "(name: string) -> i32", "documentation": "Look up a node by name from outside the parser.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/spice.flow"}, {"label": "spice_node_count", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/spice.flow"}, {"label": "spice_source", "kind": 3, "detail": "(name: string) -> i32", "documentation": "Element index of a named source, or -1.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/spice.flow"}, {"label": "spice_load", "kind": 3, "detail": "(path: string) -> bool", "documentation": "Read a deck from disk. Returns false if the file is missing or larger than\nSPICE_MAX_TEXT.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/spice.flow"}, {"label": "spice_parse", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> bool", "documentation": "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe deck\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nParse the loaded deck into stdlib/circuit.flow, then finalize it. The first\nnon-blank line is the title, as SPICE requires.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/spice.flow"}, {"label": "spice_error_line", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/spice.flow"}, {"label": "spice_skipped", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/spice.flow"}, {"label": "spice_has_tran", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> bool", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/spice.flow"}, {"label": "spice_tstep", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> f64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/spice.flow"}, {"label": "spice_tstop", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> f64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/spice.flow"}, {"label": "spice_uic", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> bool", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/spice.flow"}, {"label": "spice_has_dc", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> bool", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/spice.flow"}, {"label": "spice_dc_source", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/spice.flow"}, {"label": "spice_dc_start", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> f64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/spice.flow"}, {"label": "spice_dc_stop", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> f64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/spice.flow"}, {"label": "spice_dc_step", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> f64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/spice.flow"}, {"label": "spice_has_op", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> bool", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/spice.flow"}, {"label": "str_is_ascii_ws", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: u8) -> bool", "documentation": "ASCII whitespace that Python's int() accepts: space, tab, LF, VT, FF, CR.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/string.flow"}, {"label": "str_is_ascii_digit", "kind": 3, "detail": "(c: u8) -> bool", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/string.flow"}, {"label": "str_line_end", "kind": 3, "detail": "(s: string, start: i32) -> i32", "documentation": "Exclusive end of the line starting at `start`: the index of the first LF or\nCR, or the length, without allocating.\n`start` past the end yields the length. str_line_next skips CRLF as one\nterminator.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/string.flow"}, {"label": "str_line_next", "kind": 3, "detail": "(s: string, end: i32) -> i32", "documentation": "Start of the next line after a line that ended at `end`, or -1 if done.\nLF or CR advances one byte; CRLF advances two bytes.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/string.flow"}, {"label": "str_parse_i64_at", "kind": 3, "detail": "(s: string, start: i32) -> ParseI64", "documentation": "Parse one signed decimal token starting at `start`. Leading ASCII\nwhitespace is skipped, matching Python int(). The token is an optional\nsign and one or more digits. Overflow of i64 is an error (ok = false);\nthe value never wraps. Trailing junk is left in `end` for the caller to\ninspect.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/string.flow"}, {"label": "str_parse_i64", "kind": 3, "detail": "(s: string) -> ParseI64", "documentation": "Parse `s` as a whole, like Python int() on ASCII: leading and trailing\nwhitespace allowed, anything else is an error.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/string.flow"}, {"label": "str_parse_i32", "kind": 3, "detail": "(s: string) -> ParseI64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/string.flow"}, {"label": "str_format_i64", "kind": 3, "detail": "(buf: ptr<u8>, cap: i32, v: i64) -> i32", "documentation": "Write decimal `v` into `buf[0 .. cap)` as a NUL-terminated string.\nReturns the number of characters written (excluding NUL), or -1 if `cap`\nis too small. No heap allocation.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/string.flow"}, {"label": "str_format_i32", "kind": 3, "detail": "(buf: ptr<u8>, cap: i32, v: i32) -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/string.flow"}]}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 10, "result": [{"label": "discrete", "kind": 14, "detail": "dsys mode", "documentation": "Plant is discrete-time: `x[k+1] = A x[k] + B u[k]`."}, {"label": "sort descending", "kind": 15, "detail": "Declarative descending sort", "insertText": "${1:xs} |> sort descending", "insertTextFormat": 2, "documentation": "**`sort`** - declarative ordering (Phase 1).\n\n```flow\nxs |> sort\nxs |> sort descending\nxs |> sort by .score\nxs |> sortBy [desc .score, asc .name]\n```\nIn-place on `array<T, N>`. See docs/language/ordering.md."}, {"label": "distortion_new", "kind": 3, "detail": "(drive: f32, tone: f32, mix: f32) -> Distortion", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/effects.flow"}, {"label": "distortion_light", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> Distortion", "documentation": "Presets\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/effects.flow"}, {"label": "distortion_medium", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> Distortion", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/effects.flow"}, {"label": "distortion_heavy", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> Distortion", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/effects.flow"}, {"label": "distortion_fuzz", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> Distortion", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/effects.flow"}, {"label": "distortion_process", "kind": 3, "detail": "(dist: Distortion, input: f32) -> f32", "documentation": "Process one sample\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/effects.flow"}, {"label": "div", "kind": 3, "detail": "(a: f32, b: Dual) -> Dual", "documentation": "--- div: Division ---\n\nDual\u00f7Dual division (quotient rule). Prefer this name for operator `/` sugar.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/autodiff.flow"}, {"label": "divs", "kind": 3, "detail": "(a: Dual, b: f32) -> Dual", "documentation": "Divide Dual by scalar; named divs to avoid C div conflict historically.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/autodiff.flow"}, {"label": "divide", "kind": 3, "detail": "(a: f32, b: f32) -> f32", "documentation": "Divide a by b; returns 0 and prints on division by zero.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/math.flow"}]}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 11, "result": [{"label": "dyn.wfc field", "kind": 15, "detail": "dynamics DSL", "documentation": "**`wfc field`** - Wave Function Collapse field (experimental coupling).\n\n```flow\ndyn.wfc field layout { size 4 4  tiles 3  seed 7 }\n```", "insertText": "dyn.wfc field ${1:layout} {\n    size ${2:4} ${3:4}\n    tiles ${4:3}\n    seed ${5:7}\n}", "insertTextFormat": 2}, {"label": "gramian finite", "kind": 14, "detail": "sense Gramian binding", "documentation": "`gramian finite HZ trace -> name` / `gramian infinite HZ trace -> name` - bind controllability Gramian trace (sense block)."}, {"label": "gramian infinite", "kind": 14, "detail": "sense Gramian binding", "documentation": "`gramian finite HZ trace -> name` / `gramian infinite HZ trace -> name` - bind controllability Gramian trace (sense block)."}, {"label": "full", "kind": 14, "detail": "analyze report mode", "documentation": ""}, {"label": "function", "kind": 14, "detail": "keyword"}, {"label": "for", "kind": 14, "detail": "keyword"}, {"label": "false", "kind": 14, "detail": "keyword"}, {"label": "f32", "kind": 21, "detail": "type"}, {"label": "f64", "kind": 21, "detail": "type"}, {"label": "fabs", "kind": 3, "detail": "(x: f64) -> f64", "documentation": "Absolute value |x| for floating-point."}, {"label": "floor", "kind": 3, "detail": "(x: f64) -> f64", "documentation": "Greatest integer \u2264 x (as f64)."}, {"label": "fmod", "kind": 3, "detail": "(x: f64, y: f64) -> f64", "documentation": "Floating-point remainder of x/y."}, {"label": "flush_denormal", "kind": 3, "detail": "(x: f32) -> f32", "documentation": "Flush denormals to zero.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "feedback_is_safe", "kind": 3, "detail": "(k: f32) -> bool", "documentation": "=============================================================================\nFeedback guard\n=============================================================================\n\nA delay or reverb whose feedback coefficient reaches 1.0 never decays; past\n1.0 it grows without bound. This is the single most common way a synth\npatch turns into a hazard, so it gets a guard rather than a comment.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "feedback_guard", "kind": 3, "detail": "(k: f32) -> f32", "documentation": "Returns a coefficient that is safe to use. A magnitude at or above 1.0 is\nrefused outright and becomes 0.0, because there is no sensible substitute\nfor \"make this louder forever\". Between FEEDBACK_SOFT_MAX and 1.0 the value\nis clamped and the caller told.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "feedback_to_rt60", "kind": 3, "detail": "(k: f32, delay_seconds: f32) -> f32", "documentation": "The inverse: how long a given coefficient rings for.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "fade_gain", "kind": 3, "detail": "(t: f32) -> f32", "documentation": "Equal-power fade shape: gain = sin(pi/2 * t), so gain^2 rises like a\nquarter sine and the perceived loudness ramp is even. t = 0 gives exactly\nzero, which is what keeps the first and last sample silent.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/safety.flow"}, {"label": "freq", "kind": 3, "detail": "(midi_note: i32) -> f32", "documentation": "Shorthand: get frequency from MIDI note\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/scales.flow"}, {"label": "frame_new", "kind": 3, "detail": "(left: f32, right: f32) -> Frame", "documentation": "Create a stereo frame\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio.flow"}, {"label": "frame_mono", "kind": 3, "detail": "(value: f32) -> Frame", "documentation": "Create a mono frame (same value both channels)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio.flow"}, {"label": "frame_zero", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> Frame", "documentation": "Create a silent frame\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio.flow"}, {"label": "frame_mix", "kind": 3, "detail": "(a: Frame, b: Frame) -> Frame", "documentation": "Mix two frames together\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio.flow"}, {"label": "frame_scale", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: Frame, gain: f32) -> Frame", "documentation": "Scale a frame by a gain value\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio.flow"}, {"label": "frame_pan", "kind": 3, "detail": "(value: f32, pan: f32) -> Frame", "documentation": "Pan a mono signal (-1.0 = full left, 0.0 = center, 1.0 = full right)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio.flow"}, {"label": "frame_to_mono", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: Frame) -> f32", "documentation": "Convert stereo to mono (average)\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio.flow"}, {"label": "freq_to_period_samples", "kind": 3, "detail": "(freq: f32, rate: SampleRate) -> f32", "documentation": "Frequency to period in samples\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio.flow"}, {"label": "frame_clip", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: Frame) -> Frame", "documentation": "Clip a frame\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio.flow"}, {"label": "filter_f32", "kind": 3, "detail": "(arr: ptr<f32>, n: i32, pred: (f32) -> bool, out_n: ptr<i32>) -> ptr<f32>", "documentation": "Keep only elements where pred returns true.\nReturns a pointer; writes the filtered count to out_n.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/dsp.flow"}, {"label": "field_copy_1d", "kind": 3, "detail": "(src: ptr<f64>, dst: ptr<f64>, n: i32) -> void", "documentation": "Copy n samples from src into dst.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/dynamics/pde.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_configure", "kind": 3, "detail": "(p: i32, s: i32) -> void", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_set_particles", "kind": 3, "detail": "(n: i32, x: ptr<f64>, y: ptr<f64>, q: ptr<f64>) -> bool", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_evaluate", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> bool", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_direct_evaluate", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> bool", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_rel_field_error", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> f64", "documentation": "Paper-style relative field error: ||E_fmm - E_dir||_2 / ||E_dir||_2\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_max_rel_error", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> f64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_potential", "kind": 3, "detail": "(i: i32) -> f64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_ex", "kind": 3, "detail": "(i: i32) -> f64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_ey", "kind": 3, "detail": "(i: i32) -> f64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_nboxes", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_nleaves", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_max_level", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_time_ms", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> f64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_direct_time_ms", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> f64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_m2l_count", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> f64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_p2p_count", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> f64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_box_cx", "kind": 3, "detail": "(b: i32) -> f64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_box_cy", "kind": 3, "detail": "(b: i32) -> f64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_box_h", "kind": 3, "detail": "(b: i32) -> f64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_box_half", "kind": 3, "detail": "(b: i32) -> f64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_box_leaf", "kind": 3, "detail": "(b: i32) -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_box_level", "kind": 3, "detail": "(b: i32) -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_particle_x", "kind": 3, "detail": "(i: i32) -> f64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_particle_y", "kind": 3, "detail": "(i: i32) -> f64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_particle_q", "kind": 3, "detail": "(i: i32) -> f64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_n", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_p", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "fmm2d_s", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/fmm2d.flow"}, {"label": "font_char_width", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/font.flow"}, {"label": "font_char_height", "kind": 3, "detail": "() -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/font.flow"}, {"label": "font_glyph_row", "kind": 3, "detail": "(ch: i32, row: i32) -> u8", "documentation": "Row bit pattern for `ch` at `row` (0..6). Unknown characters render blank.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/font.flow"}, {"label": "font_pixel", "kind": 3, "detail": "(ch: i32, col: i32, row: i32) -> bool", "documentation": "True when the glyph for `ch` lights the pixel at (col, row).\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/font.flow"}, {"label": "font_text_width", "kind": 3, "detail": "(s: string, scale: i32) -> i32", "documentation": "Width in pixels of `s` drawn at `scale`, including one blank column between\ncharacters (no trailing gap).\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/font.flow"}, {"label": "font_text_height", "kind": 3, "detail": "(scale: i32) -> i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/font.flow"}, {"label": "font_int_width", "kind": 3, "detail": "(n: i32, scale: i32) -> i32", "documentation": "Digits needed to render `n` (a lone minus sign counts as one).\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/font.flow"}, {"label": "fibonacci", "kind": 3, "detail": "(n: i32) -> i32", "documentation": "Advanced mathematical functions\n\nnth Fibonacci number (F(0)=0, F(1)=1); returns 0 for n <= 0.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/math.flow"}, {"label": "factorial_big", "kind": 3, "detail": "(n: i32) -> i64", "documentation": "Factorial n! as i64; returns 1 for n <= 1. Watch for overflow on large n.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/math.flow"}, {"label": "frame_arena_create", "kind": 3, "detail": "(capacity: i64) -> FrameArena", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/memory.flow"}, {"label": "frame_arena_destroy", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: ptr<FrameArena>) -> void", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/memory.flow"}, {"label": "frame_begin", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: ptr<FrameArena>) -> void", "documentation": "Reset the frame. This is the whole deallocation.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/memory.flow"}, {"label": "frame_alloc", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: ptr<FrameArena>, size: i64) -> ptr<void>", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/memory.flow"}, {"label": "frame_alloc_i32", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: ptr<FrameArena>, count: i64) -> ptr<i32>", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/memory.flow"}, {"label": "frame_alloc_f32", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: ptr<FrameArena>, count: i64) -> ptr<f32>", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/memory.flow"}, {"label": "frame_alloc_f64", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: ptr<FrameArena>, count: i64) -> ptr<f64>", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/memory.flow"}, {"label": "frame_end", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: ptr<FrameArena>) -> void", "documentation": "Close the frame: record the high-water mark so a fixed capacity can be\nsized from a real run, and count the frame.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/memory.flow"}, {"label": "frame_used", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: FrameArena) -> i64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/memory.flow"}, {"label": "frame_remaining", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: FrameArena) -> i64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/memory.flow"}, {"label": "frame_high_water", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: FrameArena) -> i64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/memory.flow"}, {"label": "frame_count", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: FrameArena) -> i64", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/memory.flow"}, {"label": "free", "kind": 3, "detail": "(ptr: i32) -> void", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/memory_simple.flow"}, {"label": "format_hex", "kind": 3, "detail": "(value: i32) -> string", "documentation": "Helper functions\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/memory_working.flow"}, {"label": "format_hex_ptr", "kind": 3, "detail": "(ptr: i32) -> string", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/memory_simple.flow"}, {"label": "fanout2_i32", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: (i32) -> i32, g: (i32) -> i32, a: i32) -> Fanout2_i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/orchestrate.flow"}, {"label": "fanout3_i32", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: (i32) -> i32, g: (i32) -> i32, h: (i32) -> i32, a: i32) -> Fanout3_i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/orchestrate.flow"}, {"label": "fanout2_f32", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: (f32) -> f32, g: (f32) -> f32, a: f32) -> Fanout2_f32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/orchestrate.flow"}, {"label": "fanout3_f32", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: (f32) -> f32, g: (f32) -> f32, h: (f32) -> f32, a: f32) -> Fanout3_f32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/orchestrate.flow"}, {"label": "fanout2_result_i32", "kind": 3, "detail": "(f: (i32) -> Result_i32_string, g: (i32) -> Result_i32_string, a: i32) -> Fanout2_Result_i32", "documentation": "Runs both branches and keeps both results; the caller picks a join.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/orchestrate.flow"}]}
