{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 12, "result": [{"label": "dyn.ga evolve", "kind": 15, "detail": "dynamics DSL", "documentation": "**`ga evolve`** - genetic search for state-feedback gains.\n\n```flow\ndyn.ga evolve on plant over rollout -> k1 k2 {\n    population 12\n    generations 30\n    mutation 0.3\n}\n```", "insertText": "dyn.ga evolve on ${1:plant} over ${2:rollout} -> ${3:k1} ${4:k2} {\n    population ${5:12}\n    generations ${6:30}\n    mutation ${7:0.3}\n}", "insertTextFormat": 2}, {"label": "ga evolve", "kind": 15, "detail": "dynamics DSL", "documentation": "**`ga evolve`** - genetic search for state-feedback gains.\n\n```flow\ndyn.ga evolve on plant over rollout -> k1 k2 {\n    population 12\n    generations 30\n    mutation 0.3\n}\n```", "insertText": "ga evolve on ${1:plant} over ${2:rollout} -> ${3:k1} ${4:k2} {\n    population 12\n    generations 30\n    mutation 0.3\n}", "insertTextFormat": 2}, {"label": "gramian finite", "kind": 14, "detail": "sense Gramian binding", "documentation": "`gramian finite HZ trace -> name` / `gramian infinite HZ trace -> name` - bind controllability Gramian trace (sense block)."}, {"label": "gramian infinite", "kind": 14, "detail": "sense Gramian binding", "documentation": "`gramian finite HZ trace -> name` / `gramian infinite HZ trace -> name` - bind controllability Gramian trace (sense block)."}, {"label": "energy over", "kind": 14, "detail": "closed-loop energy binding", "documentation": "`energy over HZ -> name` - bind trajectory energy over a horizon (closed)."}, {"label": "generations", "kind": 14, "detail": "GA setting", "documentation": "GA generations (default 20, max 32)."}, {"label": "G", "kind": 21, "detail": "const f64"}, {"label": "GainProcessor", "kind": 22, "detail": "struct", "documentation": "=============================================================================\nExample Processors\n=============================================================================\n\n--- Gain Processor ---\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/audio/processor.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_RES_STORAGE_BUFFER", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "Backend-independent IR for multi-pass GPU programs: storage buffers,\nstorage textures, ping-pong pairs, transient resources, dispatch\ndimensions, workgroup memory/barriers, and hazard checks.\n\nThis is the Resource IR sketched in docs/project/vgpu-parity.md P2.\nFSL and @gpu can both lower into it; emitters map the same layout to\nMetal and WGSL/WebGPU.\n\nIssue #811 owns sampled textures, samplers, vertex/index buffers,\ntyped render targets, and vertex/fragment stage declarations. This\nmodule does not define those types. Bind them later by the same\ninteger resource id. Storage textures appear here because the graph\nmust name read/write access and format tags to check hazards.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_RES_STORAGE_TEXTURE", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_GRAPH_ACCESS_READ", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_GRAPH_ACCESS_WRITE", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_GRAPH_ACCESS_READ_WRITE", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_LIFE_PERSISTENT", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_LIFE_TRANSIENT", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_GRAPH_FMT_NONE", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "Storage-texture format tags used by the graph. Not the typed\ngpu.texture<Format> surface from #811.\n\nstdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_GRAPH_FMT_R32FLOAT", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_GRAPH_FMT_RG32FLOAT", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_GRAPH_FMT_RGBA16FLOAT", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_GRAPH_FMT_RGBA8UNORM", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_DIM_BUFFER", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_DIM_1D", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_DIM_2D", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_DIM_3D", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_PASS_COMPUTE", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_PASS_RENDER", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_HAZARD_STRICT", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_HAZARD_ALLOW_FEEDBACK", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_GRAPH_OK", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_GRAPH_ERR_CONFLICTING_BINDING", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_GRAPH_ERR_SAME_PASS_RW", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_GRAPH_ERR_PINGPONG_ALIAS", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_GRAPH_ERR_BAD_ACCESS", "kind": 21, "detail": "const i32", "documentation": "stdlib: lib/stdlib/gpu_graph.flow"}, {"label": "GPU_GRAPH_ERR_WORKGROUP", "kind": 21, "detail": "const 